Z||000004||DKOV||10-11-2001||01:22 AM||||Well, since we are showing of our "other" cars...  Here's a Truck and trailer I painted up for an RC race I attended in California this year...<P> <IMG SRC="http://home.att.net/~fantasyworldracing/HPI/day_two_pictures/concourse1.jpg"> <P>Not a Fiero, but a Dodge Ram pulling a trailer, carrying a Viper GT Racer.  Both of those RC cars carry a driver and FULL interior with roll cages, working dash lights, Drivers, working Head Lamps/sigals/fogs/brake lights (including the trailer), and everything was HAND BUILT including the ENTIRE trailer   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>For a TON of other pics of RC bodies I've painted, RC Racing that I participate in and racing pics, visit the Galler page at <A HREF="http://www.RCRally.com" TARGET=_blank>www.RCRally.com</A>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>So, I'm 31 and race RC Cars... So what if I own over 2 dozen of them... So what if I own a couple that cost OVER $3000...  So what?  <P>DKOV -<p>[This message has been edited by DKOV (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
